@prefix ov:      <https://data.vlaanderen.be/ns/omgevingsvergunning#> .
@prefix p-plan:  <http://purl.org/net/p-plan#> .
@prefix prov:    <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix owl:     <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

# Ontology IRI: the address of this file on GitHub, as for pplan-sosa.ttl, so that the register of
# known alignments of oslo-ld-kit (registers/alignments.ttl) can point to it.
<https://github.com/Informatievlaanderen/OSLOthema-SSNSOSA-VL/blob/main/src/main/resources/be/vlaanderen/data/ns/omgevingsvergunning/alignments/ov-pplan-prov.ttl>
    a owl:Ontology ;
    dcterms:title "AP Omgevingsvergunning alignment with P-PLAN and PROV-O (OSLOthema-SSNSOSA-VL)"@en ;
    dcterms:references
        <https://data.vlaanderen.be/ns/omgevingsvergunning#> ,
        <http://purl.org/net/p-plan#> ,
        <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/Informatievlaanderen/OSLOthema-SSNSOSA-VL/tree/main/src/main/input/omgevingsvergunning> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-11-09"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> ;
    rdfs:comment """Proposal, not part of the AP Omgevingsvergunning. Makes a procedure a plan and a
procedure step a step of that plan, a case action (zaakhandeling) an activity, and the permitted
state an entity. Through pplan-sosa.ttl a procedure and its steps are then also sosa:Procedures,
and through PROV-O plans. Order (p-plan:isPrecededBy) and sub-steps (p-plan:MultiStep) become
available to the AP without new terms (improvement point 2 in the example's README).

Deliberately not aligned, because the AP is ambiguous there (improvement point 3):
ov:JuridischWerk, ov:Rechtshandeling and their subclasses. ov:Vergunning, ov:Aanvraag and
ov:InstellingBeroep are both a case action (an activity) and, via ov:Rechtshandeling, a legal work.
Aligning ov:JuridischWerk with prov:Entity would make them inconsistent (R16). For the same reason
ov:document is not aligned with prov:generated: its domain ov:Rechtshandeling would become an
activity.

Not aligned either: ov:procedure (case to procedure). Its PROV counterpart is a qualified
association with prov:hadPlan, which has no single property to align with."""@en .

# --- Classes ---

ov:Procedure
    rdfs:subClassOf p-plan:Plan ;
    rdfs:comment "A procedure prescribes case actions in an order: a plan. Through pplan-sosa.ttl also a sosa:Procedure, through PROV-O a prov:Plan."@en .

ov:Procedurestap
    rdfs:subClassOf p-plan:Step ;
    rdfs:comment "A procedure step (a prescribed action) is a step of the procedure's plan. ov:Beroepsmogelijkheid, a subclass, becomes a step too."@en .

ov:Zaakhandeling
    rdfs:subClassOf prov:Activity ;
    rdfs:comment "A case action is something done in a case, at a time, by an agent: an activity. Not p-plan:Activity, because a case action need not correspond to a step; one that does becomes a p-plan:Activity through ov:procedurestap below."@en .

ov:VergundeToestand
    rdfs:subClassOf prov:Entity ;
    rdfs:comment "The permitted state (rights and obligations of a project at a date) is generated by a decision: an entity, the result of a sosa:Actuation."@en .

# --- Properties ---

ov:procedurestap
    rdfs:subPropertyOf p-plan:correspondsToStep ;
    rdfs:comment "The procedure step by which a case action is taken: the step the activity corresponds to. p-plan:correspondsToStep is functional, which matches the singular definition in the AP (one step per case action)."@en .
